            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-7210-python3.12",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-7210 medium vulnerability for python3.12 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`xml.parsers.expat` and `xml.etree.ElementTree` use insufficient entropy for Expat hash-flooding protection, which allows a crafted XML document to trigger hash flooding.\\r\\n\\r\\nFully mitigating this vulnerability requires both updating libexpat to 2.8.0 or later and applying this patch."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-7210",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-7210\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: python3.12\nVersion: 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.16\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3.12.list\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-7210](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-7210)",
