            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59890-python3-setuptools-whl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-59890 medium vulnerability for python3-setuptools-whl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "setuptools is a package that allows users to download, build, install, upgrade, and uninstall Python packages. Prior to 83.0.0, FileList applied MANIFEST.in exclude, global-exclude, recursive-exclude, and prune directives by matching compiled glob patterns against on-disk file names without Unicode normalization, so on macOS APFS or HFS+ an NFD file name could bypass an NFC exclusion rule and be packed into a source distribution. This issue is fixed in version 83.0.0."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59890",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-59890\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: python3-setuptools-whl\nVersion: 68.1.2-2ubuntu1.2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-setuptools-whl.list\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-59890](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59890)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-59890**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | python3-setuptools-whl  | 68.1.2-2ubuntu1.2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-setuptools-whl.list  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-59890](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59890)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/python3-setuptools-whl@68.1.2-2ubuntu1.2?arch=all\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=setuptools"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-7017-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-7017 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "HTTP::Tiny versions before 0.095 for Perl forward credential headers to cross-origin redirect targets.\n\nWhen the server returns a 3xx redirect, `_maybe_redirect` follows the `Location:` header and `_prepare_headers_and_cb` re-merges the caller's `headers` argument into the new request, without checking whether the redirect target shares an origin with the original URL. Caller-supplied `Authorization`, `Cookie` and `Proxy-Authorization` headers are therefore re-sent to whatever host the redirect names, across scheme, host or port boundaries, and including `https` to `http` downgrades that expose them in plaintext on the wire.\n\nThe HTTP::Tiny POD note that \"Authorization headers will not be included in a redirected request\" applied only to the URL-userinfo Basic-auth path, not to headers passed explicitly by the caller."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-7017",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-7017\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-7017](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-7017)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-7017**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-7017](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-7017)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41080-libexpat1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-41080 medium vulnerability for libexpat1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libexpat before 2.8.0 uses insufficient entropy, and thus hash flooding can occur via a crafted XML document."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-41080",
