            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-35195-python3-pip-whl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-35195 medium vulnerability for python3-pip-whl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Requests is a HTTP library. Prior to 2.32.0, when making requests through a Requests `Session`, if the first request is made with `verify=False` to disable cert verification, all subsequent requests to the same host will continue to ignore cert verification regardless of changes to the value of `verify`. This behavior will continue for the lifecycle of the connection in the connection pool. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.32.0."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2024-35195",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-35195\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: python3-pip-whl\nVersion: 24.0+dfsg-1ubuntu1.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-pip-whl.list\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2024-35195](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2024-35195)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-35195**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | python3-pip-whl  | 24.0+dfsg-1ubuntu1.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/python3-pip-whl.list  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2024-35195](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2024-35195)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/python3-pip-whl@24.0%2Bdfsg-1ubuntu1.3?arch=all\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=python-pip"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.6"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-76641-libexpat1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-76641 medium vulnerability for libexpat1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Expat through 2.8.3 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability that allows attackers to trigger memory corruption by processing XML with external entity parsers created via XML_ExternalEntityParserCreate. A struct size mismatch between ELEMENT_TYPE members causes storeAtts to read the attIndex member past allocated memory boundaries, resulting in failure to normalize whitespace in non-CDATA attributes or a wild pointer dereference causing a segfault. This vulnerability was introduced by the fix for CVE-2026-66046."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-76641",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-76641\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libexpat1\nVersion: 2.6.1-2ubuntu0.4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libexpat1:amd64.md5sums\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-76641](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-76641)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-76641**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libexpat1  | 2.6.1-2ubuntu0.4  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libexpat1:amd64.md5sums  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-76641](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-76641)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libexpat1@2.6.1-2ubuntu0.4?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=expat"
