            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56412-libexpat1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56412 medium vulnerability for libexpat1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libexpat before 2.8.2 does not consider XML_TOK_DATA_CHARS in doCdataSection and thus lacks handler call depth tracking for various calls from within handlers in cases of a policy violation. Thus, a use-after-free can occur. NOTE: this issue exists because of an incomplete fix for CVE-2026-50219."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-56412",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-56412\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libexpat1\nVersion: 2.6.1-2ubuntu0.4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libexpat1:amd64.md5sums\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-56412](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-56412)",
