              "id": "CVE-2026-18938-libp11-kit0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-18938 medium vulnerability for libp11-kit0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in p11-kit. A local attacker, or one with equivalent access to a reachable RPC channel, could exploit an integer overflow vulnerability. By sending specially crafted messages, the attacker can cause the system to miscalculate memory allocation for nested attributes. This leads to a memory corruption issue, specifically a heap out-of-bounds write, which can crash the p11-kit RPC parsing process, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS). This vulnerability is only exploitable on 32 bit systems."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-18938",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-18938\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libp11-kit0\nVersion: 0.25.3-4ubuntu2.1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-18938](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-18938)",
